From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:32:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 262/342] Wi-Fi: one menu entry per network; join saved
 networks again

The Deskbar network menu and the Network preferences listed a network
once for each access point and band it came through, and hidden
networks without a name: WirelessNetworkMenuItem::MergeNetworks() keeps
one entry per name, the associated access point or else the strongest.

net_server tried to join a saved network after the first scan only:
when that scan missed the network, or the join failed, there was none
until a reboot. Now every scan without a link may join, after 30 s, then
1, 2, 4 and every 8 minutes, and the AutoconfigLooper scans for it while
the interface is up; a join asked for in the last 30 s is left alone.
Auto join takes the strongest access point with the saved name. A join
for an access point other than the one a network was saved with (as
the menu's are) finds the saved settings, the password, by name.

The network settings wrote access point addresses with "%2x", a space
in place of a leading zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
